   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = 1 - y \\) with \\( f(0) = 4 \\). Find the approximation to \\( f(\\frac{3}{2}) \\) given by Euler's method, starting at \\( x = 0 \\) with three steps of equal size. Give the exact value."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         11,
         8
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The step size is \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{\\frac{3}{2} - (0)}{3} = \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (0, 4) \\) the slope is \\( -3 \\), so \\( y \\approx 4 + (\\frac{1}{2})(-3) = \\frac{5}{2} \\) at \\( x = \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            5,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{5}{2}) \\) the slope is \\( - \\frac{3}{2} \\), so \\( y \\approx \\frac{5}{2} + (\\frac{1}{2})(- \\frac{3}{2}) = \\frac{7}{4} \\) at \\( x = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            7,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "At \\( (1, \\frac{7}{4}) \\) the slope is \\( - \\frac{3}{4} \\), so \\( y \\approx \\frac{7}{4} + (\\frac{1}{2})(- \\frac{3}{4}) = \\frac{11}{8} \\) at \\( x = \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            11,
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "So \\( f(\\frac{3}{2}) \\approx \\frac{11}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            11,
            8
         ]
      }
